I found a concrete error in the literature premise: Bach’s constant 2 allows the small prime outside the subgroup to divide the modulus; the quoted bound for a unit outside is 3. The draft’s small-factor preprocessing repairs the Z application. I also found that CS assumes a character bound for the descendable set that does not follow from GRH prime-sum bounds; the stated Hölder arithmetic works if that extra bound is assumed.
